{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "rule": "no_dropped_step",
 "category": "completeness",
 "family": "no_dropped_step",
 "positiveClass": "fail",
 "definition": "no_dropped_step — a run against the earlier runs of its own case. With k of the m most recent earlier runs of the case (at most 20, newest first) doing a thing, its share is (k + 1) / (m + 2). A tool is a USUAL step when its share is three quarters or more (4 · (k + 1) ≥ 3 · (m + 2)), counting only earlier runs whose calls were recorded. The rule FAILS when this run never called a usual step; look-ups are steps like any other. An explicit empty list of tool calls is a run that made no call and is judged. The rule SKIPS when no tool calls were sent at all; below three earlier runs with recorded calls (insufficient_history); and when no tool is a usual step. A measurement: it reports and never decides the verdict. Positive = the run dropped a usual step (the rule should FAIL).",
 "source": "Authored 2026-11-10. Synthetic histories chosen so every label follows from the count stated in the note: each line of the share table on both sides, the window of twenty, an explicit empty list, runs with no recorded calls, and histories that share no step.",
 "labelling": "Labelled 2026-11-10 against the documented definition by counting, in a script that imports nothing from Iris: each note states how many of the earlier runs did the thing and the share the label follows from. A conformance family: it measures that the formula is implemented as written, not what a departure is worth. What a fire is worth is measured on AgentDojo runs and published in proof/OUTSIDE.md.",
 "labelBasis": "definition",
 "authored": "2026-11-10",
